# The image production runs. TAP-10322.
#
# `image.env` sits beside `docker-compose.prod.yml` in the deploy directory
# (`~/srv/savethedate` on it13) and holds exactly one line. It is not a secret; it is
# outside the compose file only because a digest does not exist until the image has
# been built, so it cannot be committed ahead of the release it belongs to.
#
# Pinned by tag AND digest. The tag says which release it is, for a person. The digest
# is what Docker pulls, so re-pushing the tag later cannot change what production runs.
# `scripts/prod.sh` refuses a value without a digest.
#
# You write it by hand once, when the deploy directory is first set up:
# `scripts/build-image.sh` on nlt-dev prints the line. After that the deploy unit
# rewrites it for every release, and puts the previous line back on a rollback. The
# repository part is where the next release is pulled from.
#
# SAVETHEDATE_IMAGE=<repository>:v<N>@sha256:<64 hex digits>
